\section{Ablation Studies}

\subsection{Component Ablation: TPAB vs LoRA}

To isolate TPAB's contribution, we compare three configurations: TPAB-only (35K parameters), LoRA-only (30.7M parameters), and TPAB+LoRA (Table~\ref{tab:ablation}). TPAB-only produces a small GAR improvement (+0.6 pp at d15, +0.9 pp at d25) confirming the bias does shift attention toward goal-turn positions, but at the cost of task accuracy ($-$1.2\%) because without LoRA to compensate, the attention distribution change disrupts learned patterns. LoRA-only slightly hurts GAR ($-$0.3 to $-$0.5 pp) but helps task accuracy (+0.3\%), adapting the model to the training distribution without addressing the attention mechanism. TPAB+LoRA combines both effects, but the TPAB margin over LoRA-only is +0.3 pp at d15 and +0.5 pp at d25, which is not statistically significant ($p > 0.15$).

